<div class="container">
    <h1>Dev DB Isolation, Automated Backups &amp; Availability — Implementation Plan</h1>

    <div class="last-updated">
        Status: 📋 DRAFT for review &middot; Scope: fills the gap between existing plans and a safe AI-assisted dev workflow.
        This plan does NOT re-plan K8s/Docker HA (see DOCKER_KUBERNETES_MIGRATION_STRATEGY.tt and
        PRODUCTION_DB_KUBERNETES_MIGRATION_PLAN.tt). It extends the already-built
        <code>Comserv::Util::DatabaseEnv</code> and <code>Comserv::Util::BackupManager</code> utilities.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Problem Statement (the gap)</h2>
    <p>We run AI agents and feature branches inside git worktrees (zenflow) that boot a second Catalyst
    instance per branch. The code is isolated, but the <strong>runtime database is not</strong>. The
    default environment is <code>production</code> (<code>DatabaseEnv::get_active_environment</code> returns
    <code>production</code> unless <code>ACTIVE_DB_ENVIRONMENT</code> is set), so a feature-branch server
    still resolves to the live production DB (verified: a workstation test run connected to
    <code>192.168.1.20:3307</code> = production). A "random error" or a bad agent mutation therefore writes
    to real prod data. There is also no automated, scheduled backup job — <code>BackupManager</code> exists
    for on-demand/manual backups but nothing runs it on a timer.</p>

    <h2>2. Target State</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Isolation:</strong> any non-<code>main</code> / worktree / feature instance must run against a
            <em>throwaway dev DB</em> — never production. Production is touched only by the real production container.</li>
        <li><strong>Backups:</strong> automated, scheduled, off-host backups of production (and key config) with retention
            and a tested restore path.</li>
        <li><strong>Availability:</strong> reuse the already-approved K3s/Docker HA path for the app + DB; this plan only
            adds the dev-isolation + backup automation that the HA plan assumes but does not cover.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Dev DB Isolation — Implementation</h2>
    <p>The <code>DatabaseEnv</code> system already supports <code>production|staging|dev</code> and
    <code>RemoteDB</code> already has <code>db_dev_mysql</code> and <code>db_dev_postgres</code> connection
    profiles. We only need to <strong>force</strong> the dev profile for non-production instances.</p>

    <h3>3.1 Force dev environment for worktree/feature instances</h3>
    <p>In <code>Comserv.pm</code> startup (and/or <code>DatabaseEnv::get_active_environment</code>), add an
    override: if <code>IS_DEV_WORKTREE</code> is true (already computed in <code>Root.pm:15</code>) OR the
    instance is a feature-branch server, default <code>ACTIVE_DB_ENVIRONMENT</code> to <code>dev</code> unless an
    explicit env var says otherwise. This mirrors how <code>BranchServerControl.pm</code> already distinguishes
    <code>main</code> from worktree branches.</p>

    <h3>3.2 Point dev connections at throwaway databases</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Provision a dedicated dev MariaDB/Postgres (already referenced as <code>db_dev_mysql</code> /
            <code>db_dev_postgres</code>). For agent work, seed it from a sanitized production snapshot or an
            empty schema so agents never see live PII.</li>
        <li>Set <code>ACTIVE_DB_ENVIRONMENT=dev</code> in the worktree instance's environment (e.g. in the
            <code>BranchServerControl</code> start command, alongside <code>CATALYST_DEBUG=1</code>).</li>
        <li>Document the one-liner: a feature branch server must export <code>ACTIVE_DB_ENVIRONMENT=dev</code>
            before <code>comserv_server.pl</code> boots.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>3.3 Guardrail</h3>
    <p>Keep the existing <code>DatabaseEnv</code> metadata: <code>production</code> is
    <code>confirmation_required =&gt; 1</code> and <code>read_only_recommended =&gt; 1</code>. Add a startup
    assertion that a worktree instance may NEVER bind <code>production</code> — if it detects prod binding from a
    worktree, refuse to boot (fail closed).</p>

    <h2>4. Automated Backups — Implementation</h2>
    <p><code>BackupManager</code> already archives protected files (PSGI, db_config, credentials) and can list/restore.
    It does not run on a schedule. Add a thin scheduler:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Create <code>script/backup_cron.sh</code> that calls <code>BackupManager</code> (and a
            <code>mysqldump</code>/<code>pg_dump</code> for the prod DB) and writes to
            <code>/data/nfs/backups</code> (BackupManager already prefers NFS when present).</li>
        <li>Install a cron entry (e.g. daily 02:00, retained 14 days, with off-host copy to a second Proxmox
            host or the existing backup VM 500).</li>
        <li>Production DB dump must use the existing <code>db_production_mysql</code> read credentials — never
            the app write path.</li>
        <li>Log each run to the application log + emit a health event on failure (reuse
            <code>Comserv::Util::HealthLogger</code> pattern already used by deploy failover).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Availability — Reuse, Don't Re-plan</h2>
    <p>The HA work (K3s master on stable hardware, Galera/zero-downtime cutover, Docker Compose for dev) is
    already specified in <code>DOCKER_KUBERNETES_MIGRATION_STRATEGY.tt</code> and
    <code>PRODUCTION_DB_KUBERNETES_MIGRATION_PLAN.tt</code>. This plan adds only what those assume but omit:
    <strong>dev isolation</strong> (§3) and <strong>backup automation</strong> (§4). No new HA design here.</p>

    <h2>6. Sequencing</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Phase A (this sprint, low risk):</strong> §3.1–3.3 force dev env for worktrees + fail-closed guard.
            Immediately stops agent runs from touching prod.</li>
        <li><strong>Phase B:</strong> §4 backup cron + off-host copy + restore test.</li>
        <li><strong>Phase C:</strong> align with the K3s cutover in the existing migration plans; carry the dev-isolation
            rule into the K8s dev namespace.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>7. Verification</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Boot a worktree instance with no env override → assert its DB connection is <code>db_dev_*</code>, not
            <code>db_production_mysql</code>.</li>
        <li>Boot a worktree instance and force <code>ACTIVE_DB_ENVIRONMENT=production</code> → assert it refuses to
            start.</li>
        <li>Run <code>script/backup_cron.sh</code> manually → assert a dated archive appears in
            <code>/data/nfs/backups</code> and a restore from it succeeds on a scratch DB.</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin-top:20px;"><em>Next: review, then implement Phase A (dev-isolation) as code; Phase B (backups) as
    script + cron; Phase C tracks the existing K3s plan.</em></p>
</div>
